      "book": "Anatomy_and_Physiology_2e",
      "question": "Describe indirect method.",
      "type": "unanswerable",
      "old": "编造",
      "new": "编造",
      "observed": "编造",
      "hit": null,
      "abstained": false,
      "answer": "The indirect method refers to a pathway that results in decreased activity in the cerebral cortex and therefore less motor activity.  \n\nThe indirect pathway is part of the basal ganglia circuitry and involves a longer route through the system. It includes additional connections, such as the disinhibition of the subthalamic nucleus. This pathway reinforces the normal inhibition of the thalamus, which in turn reduces the activity of the cerebral cortex. As a result, movement initiated by the cerebral cortex is diminished. The indirect pathway contrasts with the direct pathway, which leads to disinhibition of the thalamus and increased motor activity. The indirect pathway's effect on the thalamus and movement is a key aspect of how the basal ganglia regulate motor function. [p.566]"
    },
